.TITLE "attrib"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays, sets, or removes attributes assigned to files or directories. It allows for the control of __read-only__, __archive__, __system__, and __hidden__ attributes.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**attrib**
Displays the attributes of all files in the current directory.
> 

**attrib +r file**
Sets the read-only attribute for a specific file.
> __+r__ add read-only flag

**attrib -h file**
Removes the hidden attribute from a specific file.
> __-h__ remove hidden flag

**attrib +s +h folder**
Sets both the system and hidden attributes for a folder.
> __+s__ add system flag | __+h__ add hidden flag

**attrib /s /d**
Processes files and directories in the current folder and all subdirectories.
> __/s__ recursive flag | __/d__ process folders flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __attrib__ is essential for recovering files that have been hidden by malware or accidental system changes. Be careful when modifying system attributes, as it can affect OS stability.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:dir** **windows:copy**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/attrib__
